In the US this varies state by state. California Penal Code 632, the state's all-party consent statute, is the best-known example (text of the statute
(opens in new tab)
). Most EU countries expect all-party consent in practice, and workplace recordings fall under the GDPR (Regulation (EU) 2016/679 on EUR-Lex
(opens in new tab)
). Recording locally (Method 1) at least keeps the files off third-party clouds, so control over the data stays with you, but consent comes first either way. This is general information, not legal advice; rules vary by state and country.

